 ```
 
 ## API
 
-Every body is JSON. A task is `{ "id": 1, "title": "Buy milk", "done": false, "created_at": "2026-01-31T09:00:00.000Z" }`.
+Every body is JSON. A task is `{ "id": 1, "title": "Buy milk", "status": "todo", "done": false, "created_at": "2026-01-31T09:00:00.000Z" }`.
+`status` is `"todo"` (the default), `"doing"` or `"done"`. `done` is deprecated, see below.
 
 | Method and path | What it does | Answers |
 |---|---|---|
-| `GET /api/tasks` | Lists the tasks, oldest first; `?done=true` or `?done=false` keeps the done or the open ones | 200, an array of tasks |
-| `POST /api/tasks` | Creates a task from `{ "title": "…" }` | 201, the task |
+| `GET /api/tasks` | Lists the tasks, oldest first; `?status=todo`, `?status=doing` or `?status=done` keeps the tasks in that status | 200, an array of tasks |
+| `POST /api/tasks` | Creates a task from `{ "title": "…" }` and an optional `"status"` (`todo` if omitted) | 201, the task |
 | `GET /api/tasks/:id` | Reads a task | 200, or 404 `{ "error": "task not found" }` |
-| `PATCH /api/tasks/:id` | Changes `title` and / or `done` | 200, the task, or 404 |
+| `PATCH /api/tasks/:id` | Changes `title` and / or `status` | 200, the task, or 404 |
 | `DELETE /api/tasks/:id` | Deletes a task | 204, or 404 |
 
-Errors answer `{ "error": "<message>" }`.
+Errors answer `{ "error": "<message>" }`. A `status` other than `todo`, `doing` or `done`, on `POST`, `PATCH` or `?status=`, answers
+400 `{ "error": "status must be todo, doing or done" }`.
+
+## Deprecated: `done`
+
+`done` is replaced by `status` and will be removed in a later release. For one release it keeps working:
+
+- every task still has `done`, `true` exactly when its `status` is `done`;
+- `POST` and `PATCH` accept `"done": true` (status `done`) and `"done": false` (status `todo`); any other value answers
+  400 `{ "error": "done must be true or false" }`;
+- `GET /api/tasks?done=true` lists the `done` tasks and `?done=false` the `todo` and `doing` ones (any other value answers 400, same message);
+- if `status` and `done` are both sent, `status` wins.
 
 ## Layout
 
-- `src/db.ts`: opens the database and runs the migrations (`PRAGMA user_version` counts those applied).
+- `src/db.ts`: opens the database and runs the migrations (`PRAGMA user_version` counts those applied; migration 2 replaced the `done` column by `status`, `done = 1` becoming `done` and `done = 0` `todo`).
 - `src/tasks.ts`: the queries.
 - `src/app.ts`: the HTTP server and its routes.
 - `public/`: the page.
 - `test/`: the API tests, against a server on a random port with an in-memory database.
